                        "entry_id": "68b7778c-52eb-3cb4-b400-43fc68784b60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Équidé, espèce d’âne sauvage en voie de disparition et vivant en Sibérie méridionale, ainsi que dans le Turkestan et la Mongolie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "879cc43a-9677-4ec4-8ee2-2e21af900fc2",
                                "sense_id": "5d09ab14-9c99-384c-bf59-7a9e162891b2",
                                "text": "On l’appelle onagre (onos – âne, et agrios – sauvage) ou hémione (demi-âne), mais on ne le rencontre pas communément."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a1f331a2-b7c6-4739-80a3-75d79be1ad4c",
                        "source_entry_id": "68b7778c-52eb-3cb4-b400-43fc68784b60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d09ab14-9c99-384c-bf59-7a9e162891b2",
                        "target_lang_word": "asiatischer Esel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6fdcbf4d-47ba-428c-a628-0db10346fa87",
                        "source_entry_id": "68b7778c-52eb-3cb4-b400-43fc68784b60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d09ab14-9c99-384c-bf59-7a9e162891b2",
                        "target_lang_word": "Halbesel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Halbesel",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79648a01-cc48-3044-a93f-a92ce21698d5",
                                        "entry_id": "b915aea3-8418-3c87-8827-9c7308db2edd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in Asien heimisches Tier (Unpaarhufer), das mit dem Wildpferd und dem Wildesel verwandt ist und ein braunes oder gelbliches Fell hat sowie einen Quastenschwanz besitzt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d17023e3-0e16-48c2-80da-5819a213c6b3",
                                                "sense_id": "79648a01-cc48-3044-a93f-a92ce21698d5",
                                                "text": "„Bei den Halbeseln leben Hengste und Stuten in getrennten Rudeln; nur in der Brunftzeit stellen sich die Hengste bei den Stuten ein und fechten untereinander erbitterte Kämpfe aus.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "75fd1459-d5b2-442e-9991-c33e6df3e12e",
                        "source_entry_id": "68b7778c-52eb-3cb4-b400-43fc68784b60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d09ab14-9c99-384c-bf59-7a9e162891b2",
                        "target_lang_word": "onager",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "onager",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                        "entry_id": "390631cd-448d-35a1-99bd-79aa9248639b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Asiatic wild ass or hemione (Equus hemionus), an animal of the horse family native to Asia; specifically, the Persian onager, Persian wild ass, or Persian zebra (Equus hemionus onager)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d871cfa0-3860-4384-9d36-9418f1e89943",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                                "text": "[I]f the czigithai is not the ſame with the zebra, it may be the Aſiatic animal called onager or wild aſs. The onager ſhould not be confounded with the zebra; but I am uncertain whether the ſame remark is applicable to the onager and czigithai; for, from comparing the relations of travellers, it appears, that there are different kinds of wild aſſes, of which the onager is the moſt remarkable. […] The ſwiftneſs of the onager is mentioned by travellers, who remark, that he runs with ſuch rapidity as to eſcape the hunters, though mounted on horſes; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba7feaf9-b45e-4123-a60a-2b1617d6cb51",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                                "text": "The onager, or wild aſs, is ſeen in ſtill greater abundance than the wild horſe; and the peculiarities of its kind are more diſtinctly marked than in thoſe of the tame one."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "453beed3-c714-4dff-9f3d-4c9a1ff9897b",
                                                "sense_id": "f9ce8db4-9bc8-3766-9076-1b1cde5b1206",
                                                "text": "One of the onagers, however, having hurt its leg, could not be harnessed at present, and a few days' rest was necessary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fec25cf-bb83-3696-b120-75734f99eec3",
                                        "entry_id": "390631cd-448d-35a1-99bd-79aa9248639b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A military engine acting like a sling which threw stones from a bag or wooden bucket powered by the torsion from a bundle of ropes or sinews operated by machinery; a torsion catapult."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fb26d92-abef-454b-9379-112b2f9ea0de",
                                                "sense_id": "4fec25cf-bb83-3696-b120-75734f99eec3",
                                                "text": "The onager, meaning \"wild ass,\" derived its name from its powerful recoil, or kick, upon discharge; […] In addition, although Josephus described an onager in action hurling a 100-pound stone over 400 yards, most onagri achieved a shorter range than the ballista, thus exposing their crews to enemy archers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23c22365-f97c-45d9-ae98-c7f6698ddebe",
                        "source_entry_id": "68b7778c-52eb-3cb4-b400-43fc68784b60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5d09ab14-9c99-384c-bf59-7a9e162891b2",
                        "target_lang_word": "hemione",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hemione",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2fcbf1a-523d-3565-87c3-10e1f7149faf",
                                        "entry_id": "213a298d-5703-33f8-938d-8badbde9a449",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Equus hemionus, the onager or kiang, a kind of wild ass of Tibet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bba92aec-b0c2-4748-8805-b019d3babb73",
                                                "sense_id": "b2fcbf1a-523d-3565-87c3-10e1f7149faf",
                                                "text": "Its head is large, with ears smaller than those of the hemione, the shoulders thick, especially in the male, the limbs robust and stubbier than those of the hemiones and the asses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8379aa7f-b3c2-424a-803c-f6921e92be89",
                                                "sense_id": "b2fcbf1a-523d-3565-87c3-10e1f7149faf",
                                                "text": "They presumably belong to hemiones (hemiones were actually recorded from the same level at Rana Gundhai) and, in spite of some optimistic statements to the contrary, it is sometimes impossible to distinguish horses fom hemiones on isolated teeth alone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6764d24-b724-4976-86b8-20a3f5bd114b",
                                                "sense_id": "b2fcbf1a-523d-3565-87c3-10e1f7149faf",
                                                "text": "Another possible area of disagreement is that asses and hemiones are associated unequivocally in the morphological tree, but less definitely in the genetic tree: whether hemiones and African ('true') wild asses are more closely related to horses or whether they are most closely related to each other and form a separate lineage has yet to be resolved unequivocally by the DNA data, and note that in the morphological data they are united by only a single derived condition (Fig. 1.1)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "741fd1b1-8719-4559-90c4-1c7d435dc667",
